--TEST--
A `#[Json\Field(skip: true)]` property that is still a constructor parameter leaves a position no key fills, and the call that asks for a whole instance out of a document is refused — `rule:core-classes/derive-field-list`, `rule:core-api/required-optional-and-nullable`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:core-classes/derive-field-list`: `skip` takes a property off the
// contract and exempts it from the constructor-parameter requirement. The class
// stays well formed either way — it still encodes, and the program can still
// build one itself — so the refusal is of the **call** that asks for one out of
// a document, exactly as the row door refuses a `queryAs<T>`.
//
// The accepted side of the bound: a skipped property the constructor does not
// take is filled by the constructor body, so every position the decoder has to
// fill is a field and this call is fine.
#[Core\Json\Derive]
class Cached {
    public string $name;
    #[Core\Json\Field(skip: true)]
    public int $hits;

    public function constructor(string $name) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->hits = 0;
    }
}

// The refused side, one line different: the skipped property stayed a
// parameter, so there is a position the contract names no key for. A constant
// carried on a field cannot answer for it — `nvs_runtime::CodecField::default`
// fills an absent *optional key*, and this position has no field to read one
// off.
#[Core\Json\Derive]
class Stamped {
    public string $name;
    #[Core\Json\Field(skip: true)]
    public int $stamp;

    public function constructor(string $name, int $stamp) {
        $this->name = $name;
        $this->stamp = $stamp;
    }
}

// A document is a tree, so the question is asked of every deriving class the
// written one reaches rather than of its own fields alone: this call names a
// class that is fillable itself and holds one that is not.
#[Core\Json\Derive]
class Envelope {
    public Stamped $payload;

    public function constructor(Stamped $payload) {
        $this->payload = $payload;
    }
}

echo Core\Json::encode(Core\Json::decodeAs<Cached>("{\"name\":\"ada\"}")), "\n";
var $stamped = Core\Json::decodeAs<Stamped>("{\"name\":\"ada\"}");
var $envelope = Core\Json::decodeAs<Envelope>("{\"payload\":{\"name\":\"ada\"}}");
echo $stamped->name, $envelope->payload->name, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0820]: `Stamped`'s codec fills 1 of its constructor's 2 parameter(s), so `Core\Json::decodeAs` cannot build one
%A
error[E0820]: `Stamped`'s codec fills 1 of its constructor's 2 parameter(s), so `Core\Json::decodeAs` cannot build one
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
